    "title": "Sheila Hasn't Snapped Yet on B&B and That's Exactly Why Taylor Should Be Afraid",
    "text": "Photo Credit: JPI Studios The tension between Sheila and Taylor has reached a fever pitch on The Bold and the Beautiful. Their interaction has fans wondering not only if the next blow will land, but when. As Sheila’s unpredictable schemes begin to unfold, the danger to Taylor’s family has never felt more personal. Key Takeaways Sheila isn’t just reacting; she’s strategically maneuvering. The terrifying moment for Taylor is Sheila’s ability to manipulate the people that Taylor loves the most. Sheila aims to isolate her rival before delivering a final blow. At the end of Monday’s episode, Sheila (Kimberlin Brown, who is Soap Hub’s Performer of the Month for March) picked up a pizza cutter to torture Taylor (Rebecca Budig). This scene showed that this domestic object is more than just a weapon. It’s a symbol of Sheila’s ability to make a threat without committing a crime. This keeps viewers on edge for April sweeps, while keeping Sheila in that dangerous gray area where she hasn’t killed anyone yet. B&B fans are already aware that Sheila is a master of the slow burn. The pizza cutter moment from Monday’s episode might not be the beginning of a bloodbath. Rather, it’s an opening salvo into a psychological war designed to drive Taylor to the breaking point, in time for May sweeps. Sheila’s Slow Burn Strategy Revealed So far, Taylor is convinced that she has a future with Deacon (Sean Kanan). She told Sheila that they’re in love. However, in Sheila’s mind, she has a happy marriage with Deacon. She believes he still loves her, even though he’s been seeing Taylor behind her back. If Sheila were to attack Taylor now, she’d lose her reformed status and her marriage to Deacon immediately. It’s better for Sheila to use the pizza cutter to intimidate Taylor into ending the affair. Sheila still thinks she has the upper hand because she’s married to Deacon. Later this month, we’ll enter the time period when soaps ramp up the stakes. Will Sheila Carter Win? There could be a “cat-and-mouse” game between Sheila and Taylor throughout April to keep the ratings high and lead in May sweeps. Taylor is a world-renowned psychiatrist who can usually keep her composure. Sheila knows the best way to make Taylor look “crazy” or “paranoid” to Ridge (Thorsten Kaye) and the rest of the family. Using something as harmless as a pizza cutter is the perfect way to gastlight her. There’s no doubt that Taylor will be on high alert now. How will Sheila get her revenge? Will she strike back at Taylor or walk away?",
